# Verification and testing

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` sections 6 and 7; details in `rules/verification-and-diagnosis.md`.
Apply when running tests, judging a result or diagnosing a failure.

- Evidence must match the claim; always state what the check does not prove.
- Prove the run was valid (target, input, own output, no early infrastructure failure) before
  calling pass or fail.
- Runs sharing a resource are compared one after another, in the same order.
- Failure attribution: change surface first, existing control run, normalized trace diff,
  quantities as evidence, then a positive control. Say whether you have proof or correlation.
